      "costUsd": 0.0260295,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the rate graph from the end of the last video. Water flows into this rainwater tank at two t times e to the t squared litres per second, so the graph shows how fast the water is coming in, not how much is there. A question could ask how much water flows in during the first second. It could ask for the volume at any time t. Another question could ask for an area, or give you only ay table of readings. Every one of those needs an integral, but not the same one. So how do you tell which integral a question needs?"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-02",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-g02/scene-02.wav",
      "durationInFrames": 1539,
      "worstWordGap": {
