      "loggedRequestAttempts": 0,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 0,
      "outputTokens": 0,
      "costUsd": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "So find the integral from zero to one of two t, times e to the t squared. Look inside first. The inside is t squared, and its derivative, two t, is out the front. So a primitive is e to the t squared. At one, that's e, and at zero it's one, so the water added is e minus one litres, about one point seven two. The rate is never negative here, so this is also the area under the curve. On the tank's gauge, that's the water added in the first second."
    },
