      "outputTokens": 1643,
      "costUsd": 0.0148975,
      "pronunciationText": "Now a quick sort. For each question, decide which kind it is, but don't work it out yet. First, a town's population, in thousands, grows at three e to the half t per year, and it starts at ten. Find the population at time t. Think for three seconds. It asks for a function, so integrate with plus C, and the start fixes the C. Second, find the area between y equals sine x and the x-axis, from zero to two pi. The curve crosses the axis at pi, so split there. The integral alone is zero, but the area is four. Third, estimate the integral from zero to one of e to the minus x squared. This time there's a formula, but it has no primitive you can write down in this course, so it's the trapezoidal rule again."
    },
